    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43966" root="&#xA;                        نسو and نسى&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            6
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَنَاسَاهُ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He pretended that he had forgotten
it:</i> (S, KL, * TA:) and (TA) <i>he forgot it;</i>
(MA, KL, * TA;) like ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَسِيَهُ</span></b> : (TA:) [or] <i>he
constrained himself to dismiss it from his mind.</i>
(MA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُنُوسِىَ</span>
                        <i>It</i> (a word or the like) <i>was
forgotten by degrees.</i> (Occurring often in the
larger Lexicons.)

